---
// src/components/Faq.astro
---

<section class="mt-14 pt-8 border-t border-white/[0.06] space-y-2">
  <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500 mb-4 text-center">
    Questions & Answers
  </div>

  <div class="divide-y divide-white/[0.06] border-y border-white/[0.06]">
    <details class="group py-3.5 transition-colors">
      <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <span>Do I need to create an account?</span>
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2 leading-relaxed pr-6">
        No. There are no sign-ups, logins, or subscriptions. You can paste a link, trim your clip, and download it right away.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="group py-3.5 transition-colors">
      <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <span>How long can my clips be?</span>
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2 leading-relaxed pr-6">
        You can trim clips up to 10 minutes long from videos of any length, including multi-hour podcasts and livestreams.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="group py-3.5 transition-colors">
      <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <span>Does trimming reduce video quality?</span>
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2 leading-relaxed pr-6">
        No. Your clip is exported in the video's original resolution (up to 4K) without re-compression or blurring.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="group py-3.5 transition-colors">
      <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <span>Are my videos stored or uploaded anywhere?</span>
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2 leading-relaxed pr-6">
        Never. All trimming runs directly inside your web browser. Your video bytes are never saved on a server.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
